  "question": {
    "text": "In a face centred cubic lattice, atoms of A form the corner points and atoms of B form the face centred points. If two atoms of $\\mathrm{A}$ are missing from the corner points, the formula of the ionic compound is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NMALx",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{AB}_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QAzD5",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{AB}_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jrzHg",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{A}_2 \\mathrm{~B}_5$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zWkge",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{AB}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "A form corner points and two atoms of A are missing from corner\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\therefore \\quad & \\text { Atoms at corner }(\\mathrm{A})=6 \\times \\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{3}{4} \\\\\n& \\text { Atoms at face centre }(\\mathrm{B})=6 \\times \\frac{1}{2}=3 \\\\\n\\therefore & \\mathrm{A}_{3 / 4} \\mathrm{~B}_3 \\text { i.e., } \\mathrm{AB}_4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
